hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1667","Narrated to us Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, (who said) narrated to us 'Abd al-A'la, (who said) Sa'id al-Jurayri informed us. And it was also narrated to us Abu Hashim Ziyad ibn Ayyub, (who said) narrated to us Isma'il, (who said) Sa'id al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id (RA), who said:\n\n\We had not long returned from the conquest of Khaybar when we came upon a field of garlic. We ate from it in abundance"," for some of us were hungry. Then we went to the mosque"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) noticed the odor. He said"," 'Whoever has eaten from this foul tree must not come near us in our mosque.'\n\nThe people said"," 'It is forbidden! It is forbidden!' This reached the Prophet (ﷺ)"," so he said"," 'O people"," I have not been given the authority to forbid what Allah has made lawful. Rather"," this is a tree whose odor I dislike.'\n\nThis is the narration of Abu Hashim.\n\nAbu Musa added at the end of his narration"," 'Indeed"," the angels come to me"," and I dislike that they should smell its odor.'\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
